## Open Redirection
Open Redirection is a security flaw that occurs when a web application redirects users to a URL specified in an
invalidated parameter. Attackers exploit this vulnerability to redirect users to malicious sites.
In the provided PHP code snippet:
use Symfony\Bundle\FrameworkBundle\Controller\AbstractController;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Request;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;
use Symfony\Component\HttpKernel\Attribute\MapQueryParameter;
